---
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// THE SITE FOOTER — the first shared component in this repo.
//
// Created 2026-08-29 with exactly ONE consumer: src/pages/events.astro. The
// other six carriers still hold their own copy and convert one at a time; this
// file is not finished, it is started.
//
// ⚠ THE MARKUP IS events.astro's, VERBATIM, AND THAT CHOICE IS THE WHOLE POINT.
// Of the three Astro carriers, events.astro was the only one holding NEITHER
// known drift: index.astro writes a bare `#programs` where everything else
// writes `/#programs`, and NewsLayout links the SunshineFM newsletter where the
// others link News RSS. Starting from events means the component is born in the
// canonical form and neither drift has to be represented yet. Starting from
// either other file would have baked a per-surface variant into the shared
// thing on day one.
//
// ⚠ NO PROPS, AND KEEP IT THAT WAY UNTIL A REAL SECOND CASE ARRIVES. There is
// no interpolation, no Astro.props, no conditional and no active state in here,
// because events.astro needed none. A footer that takes a prop on its first
// page takes more on its seventh, and the two known drifts are the temptation:
//   · `#programs` vs `/#programs` — MEASURED on production, these resolve to the
//     IDENTICAL url on the homepage (`…org/#programs` both ways), because the
//     homepage is served at `/`. The bare form is not required, it is merely
//     equivalent on the one page it appears on. So this is a copy change when
//     index.astro converts, NOT a prop. (⚠ On the LOCAL static preview the
//     homepage is `/index.html`, where the two genuinely differ — a local check
//     will show a difference production does not have.)
//   · the SunshineFM newsletter vs News RSS — a real editorial difference per
//     surface, and the only candidate for a prop. It is not decided here, and
//     it does not have to be until NewsLayout converts.
//
// ⚠ MARKUP ONLY — NO <style> BLOCK AND NO FONT REQUEST, DELIBERATELY. The
// footer's CSS already lives in public/styles/shared.css and src/styles/
// chrome.css, and each converting page keeps its own .footer__desc /
// .footer__col-label rules. More to the point: src/components/ is OUTSIDE gate
// 6's surface sweep and gate 7's font sweep (both walk src/pages and
// src/layouts only). A <style> block here would never be checked for
// duplicating shared.css, and a font family requested here would never be
// checked for coverage. That gap is known and logged; until it is closed, this
// component must not be the place either of those things lives.
//
// GATE 5 DOES see this file: src/components joined footerSearchRoots in
// 6daeae8, and the completeness check resolves imports transitively, so
// events.astro passes by REACHING this footer rather than by carrying one. The
// positioning line below is verified against src/data/positioning.ts on every
// build — edit it here and the build tells you.
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
---

